# ZIMDNS example DNSSEC signing key.
#
# One `<algorithm> <secret>` pair per line. The secret is base64: the ECDSA
# private scalar, or the Ed25519 seed. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# This is the Ed25519 key published as an example in RFC 8080 section 6.1, so
# nothing secret is committed here. Replace it before signing anything real:
#
#   ed25519 <32-byte base64 seed>
#   ecdsap256sha256 <32-byte base64 private scalar>
#   ecdsap384sha384 <48-byte base64 private scalar>
#
# The DNSKEY is always owned by the zone apex (RFC 4034 section 5.1.1), so a
# zone name in this file could only ever be wrong. This build signs one zone
# with this key and refuses RSA (IANA algorithms 5, 7, 8, 10) and Ed448 (RFC
# 8080 algorithm 16): the standard library has no primitive for either.
ed25519 DSSF3o0s0f+ElWzj9E/Osxw8hLpk55chkmx0LYN5WiY=